Lets a resource transform fail a request instead of returning a URL. A
transform that adds a credential or routes through a proxy had no way to stop
a request when it couldn't do that, so the request went out with its original
URL (https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/779). A failed
request is never sent. When the error's reason allows a retry, the retry calls
the transform again instead of loading the original URL.
Upstream: not proposed

